# CODEOWNERS template for product repos. GitHub ignores this file here because of its name.
#
# To use it in a product repo:
#   1. Copy it to .github/CODEOWNERS.
#   2. Replace every @harness-owner with the reviewing user, or with a team (@org/team) at work.
#   3. Add a ruleset on the default branch that requires review from code owners, with the owner
#      as a bypass actor for pull requests. docs/hooks.md has the settings.
#
# Agents can't change guardrail files: the guardrail path check fails their PRs. Owning the
# guardrails here means Dependabot's PRs and the owner's own PRs need a code owner too. Agents may
# change the product and architecture docs, but only with the owner's approval.
#
# Paths are case-sensitive here, unlike the path check. Each guardrail is listed in the casing
# .NET tools look for; the path check still catches any other casing in an agent PR.
#
# Keep this file in step with isGuardrailPath in plugins/factory-harness/hooks/rules/guardrail-files.mjs.
# The CI tests fail if a guardrail path isn't owned here.

# Guardrail files, at any depth.
.editorconfig                   @harness-owner
*.globalconfig                  @harness-owner
*.runsettings                   @harness-owner
Directory.Build.props           @harness-owner
Directory.Build.targets         @harness-owner
Directory.Packages.props        @harness-owner
nuget.config                    @harness-owner
NuGet.config                    @harness-owner
NuGet.Config                    @harness-owner
global.json                     @harness-owner
**/.config/dotnet-tools.json    @harness-owner
stryker-config.json             @harness-owner
stryker-config.yml              @harness-owner
stryker-config.yaml             @harness-owner
.github/                        @harness-owner
.claude/                        @harness-owner
*.ArchitectureTests/            @harness-owner

# Product and architecture docs. Agents may propose changes; the owner approves them.
/docs/product.md                @harness-owner
/ARCHITECTURE.md                @harness-owner
/docs/adr/                      @harness-owner
